config FREETZ_PACKAGE_FREETZ_PROXY
	bool "freetz-proxy 0.1 - HTTPS multi-service reverse proxy CGI"
	default n
	depends on FREETZ_INSTALL_BASE
	help
		CGI binary that acts as an HTTPS-to-HTTP reverse proxy for
		multiple local services, allowing secure access via the
		FritzBox built-in HTTPS web interface.

		URL scheme:
		  https://fritz.box/cgi-bin/freetz_proxy/
		    → HTML index of all configured services
		  https://fritz.box/cgi-bin/freetz_proxy/freetz/
		    → Freetz-EVO (port from /mod/etc/conf/mod.cfg)
		  https://fritz.box/cgi-bin/freetz_proxy/myapp/
		    → custom service on configured port

		Services are configured in /mod/etc/conf/freetz-proxy.cfg:
		  freetz=81
		  myapp=9999

		The "freetz" service is auto-added from MOD_HTTPD_PORT in
		/mod/etc/conf/mod.cfg when absent from the config file.

		Location: response headers are rewritten so that upstream
		redirects stay within the HTTPS proxy URL.

